From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yusuke Shinozaki <vin.bleu@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 12 Sep 2026 09:03:57 +0900
Subject: net: stmmac: tc956x: select the MAC speed before the first PMA init

The MAC speed selector (EMAC_CTL.SP_SEL) is only programmed from
tc956x_fix_mac_speed(), i.e. after phylink has seen the link come up.
Out of reset SP_SEL holds a value that is neither an SGMII rate nor
2500BASE-X.

For 2500BASE-X that is harmless: the PHY drives the link and
fix_mac_speed() then programs SP_SEL.  For SGMII it is fatal: the
in-band autonegotiation between the XPCS and the PHY cannot complete
while SP_SEL is invalid, phylink never sees the link, fix_mac_speed()
is never called, and the port stays without carrier forever.  On a
Radxa Dragon Q8B (QPS615) a port whose first link after boot is SGMII
(1000/100/10 Mbit/s partner) never links; a port that first linked at
2.5 Gbit/s links fine at 1 Gbit/s afterwards because SP_SEL was
programmed by then.

Program SP_SEL for the interface's native rate (SGMII: 1000,
2500BASE-X: 2500) in tc956x_mac_enable(), before the PMA is initialised
and the XPCS reset is released.  fix_mac_speed() still reprograms it
with the negotiated speed once the link is up.

Tested on a Radxa Dragon Q8B (Armbian 7.2.3-edge-sc8280xp) against a
Netgear M4250 (1000BASE-T) and a 2.5GBASE-T switch: both ports now link
at 1000/100/10 and 2500 from cold boot without any intervention.

Signed-off-by: Yusuke Shinozaki <vin.bleu@gmail.com>
---
 .../ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/dwmac-tc956x.c    | 29 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 29 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/dwmac-tc956x.c b/drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/dwmac-tc956x.c
index 81c0bd4..b1cf2e6 100644
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/dwmac-tc956x.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/dwmac-tc956x.c
@@ -337,10 +337,34 @@ static int tc956x_mac_configure(struct tc956x_data *td,
 	return 0;
 }
 
+/*
+ * Speed to select before the first link comes up.
+ *
+ * EMAC_CTL.SP_SEL resets to a value that is neither an SGMII rate nor
+ * 2500BASE-X.  For SGMII the in-band autonegotiation cannot complete
+ * until SP_SEL selects an SGMII rate, so the link never comes up and
+ * fix_mac_speed() (which is what programs SP_SEL) is never called.
+ * Select the interface's native rate here; fix_mac_speed() reprograms
+ * it once the PHY reports the negotiated speed.
+ */
+static int tc956x_mac_initial_speed(phy_interface_t interface)
+{
+	switch (interface) {
+	case PHY_INTERFACE_MODE_SGMII:
+		return SPEED_1000;
+	case PHY_INTERFACE_MODE_2500BASEX:
+		return SPEED_2500;
+	default:
+		return -EOPNOTSUPP;
+	}
+}
+
 static void tc956x_mac_enable(struct tc956x_data *td)
 {
 	const struct tc956x_chip *chip = td->auxbus_data->chip;
+	phy_interface_t interface = td->plat->phy_interface;
 	u32 id = td->auxbus_data->mac_id;
+	int speed;
 
 	tc956x_clock_enable(chip, id, MAC_CLOCK_TX);
 	tc956x_clock_enable(chip, id, MAC_CLOCK_RX);
@@ -349,6 +373,11 @@ static void tc956x_mac_enable(struct tc956x_data *td)
 		tc956x_clock_enable(chip, id, MAC_CLOCK_RMII);
 
 	tc956x_reset_deassert(chip, id, MAC_RESET_MAC);
+
+	speed = tc956x_mac_initial_speed(interface);
+	if (speed > 0)
+		tc956x_mac_configure(td, interface, speed);
+
 	tc956x_pma_init(td);
 	tc956x_reset_deassert(chip, id, MAC_RESET_XPCS);
 }
-- 
